WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.414
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Sunday, November first.

2
00:00:04.414 --> 00:00:11.937
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:11.937 --> 00:00:14.418
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.418 --> 00:00:24.067
Today: a threat warning in Moscow, flooding in the Galápagos, Ebola testing in Nigeria, violence in India's Manipur state, and fighting near Aden in Yemen.

5
00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:25.459
We start in Russia.

6
00:00:25.459 --> 00:00:26.533
The U.S.

7
00:00:26.533 --> 00:00:28.531
State Department says the U.S.

8
00:00:28.531 --> 00:00:39.205
Embassy in Moscow was aware of a credible threat of a mass casualty event yesterday at the Tsaritsyno Museum Reserve in Moscow, and that the U.S. government was coordinating with Russian authorities on a response.

9
00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:42.372
Canada's travel advisory service relayed the alert.

10
00:00:42.372 --> 00:00:51.082
The independent Russian outlet Meduza reports Russia's F S B security service said it received a U.S. warning about a terror plot in Moscow.

11
00:00:51.082 --> 00:00:52.672
Next, Ecuador.

12
00:00:52.672 --> 00:00:53.765
The U.S.

13
00:00:53.765 --> 00:01:02.283
State Department says heavy rains flooded homes on Santa Cruz Island in the Galápagos, and that local authorities declared an emergency on Friday, October thirtieth.

14
00:01:02.283 --> 00:01:09.765
It says a house collapsed, power is out in the island's highlands, and the road between Puerto Ayora and Bellavista is closed.

15
00:01:09.765 --> 00:01:14.831
The State Department also says Baltra airport has temporarily suspended operations.

16
00:01:14.831 --> 00:01:16.108
Canada and the U.K.

17
00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:21.231
Foreign Office both updated their Ecuador advice for the flooding.

18
00:01:21.231 --> 00:01:22.653
Turning to Nigeria, and an Ebola update.

19
00:01:22.653 --> 00:01:29.166
Nigeria's Centre for Disease Control said two suspected Ebola cases were identified in the northeast and isolated.

20
00:01:29.166 --> 00:01:36.350
It later said samples from the two people, in Yola, Adamawa State, tested negative after two rounds of testing.

21
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:46.779
Separately, BBC Africa reports the Ebola treatment centre in Mongbwalu, in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, has discharged its last patients with confirmed Ebola.

22
00:01:46.779 --> 00:01:48.210
Next, India.

23
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:52.985
Reuters reports five people were killed in fresh ethnic violence in Manipur state.

24
00:01:52.985 --> 00:02:00.694
The New Indian Express reports police said three Kuki men were killed in a gunfight between rival armed groups in Noney district yesterday.

25
00:02:00.694 --> 00:02:01.848
And in Yemen.

26
00:02:01.848 --> 00:02:13.978
The Institute for the Study of War assesses that recent Houthi attempts to advance from Taiz governorate into Lahij governorate may indicate the Houthis are trying to set conditions to besiege or capture the city of Aden.

27
00:02:13.978 --> 00:02:18.663
It says government-aligned forces reportedly recaptured some areas in Lahij.

28
00:02:18.663 --> 00:02:20.865
Now a few quick notes by region.

29
00:02:20.865 --> 00:02:36.129
In the Middle East, the Institute for the Study of War and the Critical Threats Project report Iran's Supreme Leader, Mojtaba Khamenei, directed Iran's three top military commanders to prepare to retaliate against any U.S. strikes by expanding Iran's list of targets.

30
00:02:36.129 --> 00:02:43.174
Reuters reports Iranian envoys met Qatari mediators as the threat of U.S. strikes after the midterm elections looms.

31
00:02:43.174 --> 00:02:57.174
In Africa, Libya's National Oil Corporation said an armed group forcibly shut a valve on the main crude oil pipeline linking the Hamada field to the Zawiya refinery, on Friday, October thirtieth, according to local and regional media.

32
00:02:57.174 --> 00:03:01.859
And in Europe, an update on the evacuation from Oleshky in southern Ukraine.

33
00:03:01.859 --> 00:03:09.882
Radio Free Europe reports hundreds of residents have now arrived in Ukrainian-controlled territory, helped by a convoy of twenty five buses.

34
00:03:09.882 --> 00:03:14.556
Reuters reports four planes carrying evacuated residents landed in Belarus.

35
00:03:14.556 --> 00:03:15.925
That's today's brief.

36
00:03:15.925 --> 00:03:24.203
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

37
00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:32.437
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

38
00:03:32.437 --> 00:03:34.549
This brief is digitally narrated.

39
00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:35.478
Questions?

40
00:03:35.478 --> 00:03:38.950
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

41
00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.972
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
